  id: poi-a
  title: "Brass-Number Arrest at Harrow & Tincture"
  situation: "Gaslight sputters over the Black Puddle. Two Wardens with brass collar-numbers try to drag Apothecary Harrow from his narrow shop; a third blocks the door, eyeing a locked oak cabinet. Mill neighbours shout that Harrow sells cheap cough draughts. Harrow swears the black tincture talk is a frame. The street can still tip either way. (11.1 POI A)"
  poi: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1d3d9d0cb6654077ac21992cc277ad91, type: 2}
  scene: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7f9b1d3e5a6c4d0e2f4a6b8c0d2e4f6a, type: 2}
  primaryAxis: 2
  secondaryAxis: 1
  options:
  - name: "Defend Harrow"
    axes:
    - 2
    - 1
    approaches:
    - 5
    - 1
    - 2
    dialogueOptions:
    - defend
    - threaten
    - force
    cost: "Warden heat; a threat costs the Wardens' Attitude either way (10.4 §5); freeing him by force is a fight with the three Wardens, and a fight lost lets them take him"
    consequence: "The shop stays open tonight; Harrow owes a debt"
    opens: "Cheap medicine, a later mixture clue, Veinmarket's fighter at the invasion (11)"
    closes: "Easy Warden mentorship; clean legal cover"
    failure: "Rebuffed: the player learns the cabinet mattered more than Harrow, and may still choose otherwise"
    residue:
    - aftermath.harrow.defended
    - debt.veinmarket
    - debt.harrow
    countsAsWithdraw: 0
